/* =====================================================================================
   DM-A1  |  Attribute Checks - Data Type & Format Preserved  (MAXIMUS)
   Dates, decimals and trailing spaces not truncated or altered on load. Pass criterion: types & formats match source (status = PASS on every row).

   Check ID: DM-A1
   Category: Attribute checks
   Sign-off criterion: Data type & format preserved
   Method: (a) per project: RAW column type / length / scale vs satellite column
       (INFORMATION_SCHEMA); (b) per satellite: sampled satellite values vs the
       UNTRANSFORMED RAW value, each difference classified
   Pass criteria / tolerance: Types & formats match source; only differences explained
       by a documented model rule
   Owner: LUMIQ
   Vault location: BAGIC_PREPROD_CURATED_DB.BGIL_DATA_MODEL
   Maximus RAW: BAGIC_PROD_MIRROR_DB.MAXI_RAW
   Opus RAW (test): BAGIC_PREPROD_CURATED_DB.UTILS (prod:
       BAGIC_PROD_MIRROR_DB.OPUS_GG_DWHSTAGE)
   Scope: Every standard + augmented satellite of maximus_partner_dv_dbt and
       opus_partner_dv_dbt, one section per project-satellite. Satellite rows are scoped by
       the RECORD_SOURCE each feed writes.
   Sample: Deterministic: the first 100 keys per RECORD_SOURCE ordered by hash key
       (re-runnable, same keys every time). Change SAMPLE_N in gen_dm_a.py to the agreed
       sample size and regenerate.
   Latest row rule: Satellite: max LOAD_DATETIME per key (per key + child key for
       multi-active). RAW: rows at the max load timestamp per key; ties are kept and a
       value matches if it equals any tied RAW row.
   Classes (b): EXACT, BLANK_TO_NULL, TRIMMED, CASE_CHANGED, NUMBER_FORMAT_CHANGED,
       DATE_FORMAT_CHANGED, TRUNCATED, VALUE_DIFFERS
   model_rule: What the dbt expression does to the RAW column: trim / nullif
       (blank->NULL) / case (upper/lower) / conv (type conversion, regexp). A class is
       accepted only when the rule explains it; TRUNCATED always fails.
   Documented exception: Leading / trailing space removal and blank -> NULL are an
       accepted, documented exception to 'trailing spaces not altered': the stg_ models
       apply nullif(trim(col::varchar), '') by design and this rule is NOT to be changed.
       TRIMMED / BLANK_TO_NULL counts on columns whose model_rule contains trim / nullif
       therefore PASS and are reported as evidence of the exception only.
   Project in this file: MAXIMUS

   GENERATED by validation/tools/gen_dm_k.py from the current dbt models -- edit the generator,
   not this file. The queries are IDENTICAL to those in the matching .docx.

   Revision notes:
   - Generated 2026-10-13 from the current maximus_partner_dv_dbt models by
     validation/tools/gen_dm_a.py (reuses the gen_dm_k.py staging parser and hash
     formula).
   - This file: MAXIMUS only (98 satellites, standard + augmented); 91 have mapped
     payload, 123 RECORD_SOURCE groups, 639 mapped (group, column) pairs. The other
     project is in the sibling file (OPUS).
   - Lineage handled: stg_ direct, Maximus thin wrappers, Maximus unpivot arms (each
     arm's filter kept), Opus stitch views (recomputed from RAW with the stitch macro's
     coalesce priority and tie-break), OBJECT satellites (per-source-table entries),
     multi-active satellites (per child key).
   - Sections marked NA load only hard-coded NULL padding or a disabled placeholder.
   - DM-A1: trailing / leading space trimming and blank -> NULL in staging are a
     documented exception (agreed 2026-10-13); the staging trim rule stays unchanged.
   ===================================================================================== */


